.r8-cols.r9-single { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); max-width: 780px; }

/* 5 · Kill a stray vertical scrollbar in the sub-tab strip.
   r8 sets `overflow-x: auto`, and per spec a non-visible value on one axis
   forces the other to compute to `auto`. `.r8-tab`'s `margin-bottom: -1px`
   (the underline-bleed trick) pushes exactly 1px past the strip's content box,
   which is enough to trigger a vertical scrollbar — it painted a full widget in
   the strip band and ate 14px of width, truncating the sub-labels early.
   Nothing real is clipped: the only overflow is that intentional 1px bleed.
   Horizontal scrolling still works. */
.r8-strip { overflow-y: hidden; }

